# Curation verdicts: entries the mesh must never capture again.
#
# Each line is sha256("<project>/<agents|commands|skills>/<relative-path>") — a
# one-way digest, so this file records the verdicts without publishing a roster of
# project names and their internal tooling. capture_file() hashes the candidate path
# and looks it up here; /promote appends the digest of anything it rejects.
#
# Two reasons a verdict lands here: the tool is project-local (it stays in its home
# project with its context), or its reusable core was already generalized into the
# library, so re-capturing the original would just churn.
#
# To re-admit a file, drop its digest:
#   printf '%s' '<project>/<category>/<path>' | shasum -a 256 | cut -d' ' -f1

